id: pm-github-sync-host-compatibility
title: Preflight gated sync and closeout host compatibility
description: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/279"
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: changelog-unreleased,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#279"
created_at: "2026-11-26T08:22:23.276Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-26T12:01:16.837Z"
assignee: codex
claim_principal: codex
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Reject unsupported or unreadable installed pm CLI versions before both workflows run tracker commands. Report the release, host, tested range and pin remedy. Preserve mutation refusal details in apply failures."
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-26T08:24:45.083Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced against published packages with the real pm CLI 2026.11.23 and a synthetic GitHub REST issue. Preview passed on pm-github 2026.11.15 and 2026.11.25. The older apply failed in github-import-owner before create, and the newer apply imported one issue. The linked pm-rl run failed in preview, while the other three linked runs failed in apply. Plan: gate both workflows just after npm ci, read the installed local launcher, derive the range from the selected release metadata and preserve guard failures at the shared hook boundary."
  "2026-11-26T08:28:47.956Z",codex-agent,"Both workflows preflight the exact caller-local launcher with no global fallback. The release-selected npm metadata records a floor exercised by the packed minimum-SDK test and an inclusive ceiling from the exact lockfile-installed development host. The older release records 2026.10.23 through 2026.11.6. A supported version continues silently. Unreadable CLI or release evidence stops the job without leaking process output. The shared ownership/closeout hook wrapper preserves raw thrown detail across the SDK error boundary, and closeout redacts it before returning a report."
  "2026-11-26T08:56:58.031Z",codex-agent,"The first linked run executed 1,350 tests with 1,346 passes. Four inventory tests identified stale generated anchors shifted by the workflow and guard changes. Regenerated the ownership inventory from the changed source and will verify the focused inventory file again."
  "2026-11-26T08:58:50.231Z",codex-agent,"Disposable behavioral reverts gave the expected failures. Removing both preflight steps failed 28 tests. Bypassing refusals failed 20 tests covering old, newer, prerelease, unreadable and unverified-range cases. Excluding supported endpoints failed four tests. Removing release-evidence transport failed both resolver tests. Removing the alert allowlist entry failed its shell test. Reverting each of the four caller and recovery documents independently failed the documentation contract. Bypassing guard wrapping failed the import, closeout and packed npm/Bun tests. Removing closeout guard reporting failed its redacted refusal test. Restored controls passed 45 workflow, metadata and alert tests plus all three guard tests."
  "2026-11-26T08:59:32.666Z",codex-agent,"Local targeted validation complete. The linked 42-file Node run reported 1,350 tests, 1,346 passes and four stale generated inventory anchors. The regenerated inventory check and the two-file rerun passed, 37 of 37, including all four initial failures. Typecheck, test build, lint, docstrings and the precommit privacy and identity scan passed. The packed regression exercised npm and native Bun against a non-git tracker and retained the apply guard reason in both JSON and the default TOON-facing CLI path. Coverage and full release gates are reserved for CI."
  "2026-11-26T09:22:35.192Z",codex-agent,"Node 22 on 36499f00062177adc6c793630b4ea0c300592a42 passed the new behavioral tests and failed the existing repository-wide publish-attestation test. The verifier parsed JavaScript from a heredoc as additional shell lines. The workflow now passes the identical JavaScript as one quoted Node argument. The existing verifier and generated ownership inventory check both pass with this transport. Exact-head run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/45788120995/job/139799988186."
  "2026-11-26T09:24:16.815Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI on the first commit reported 2,182 of 2,183 tests passing in each Node job, with the same sole publish-attestation failure. The repaired workflow transport passes the unchanged verifier and 53 of 53 linked attestation, workflow, alert and metadata tests. Both static workflow contracts passed. Reverting the transport in a disposable checkout reproduced all ten verifier violations. Restoring it passed the verifier again. Typecheck, lint and the generated ownership inventory check passed."
  "2026-11-26T10:15:42.244Z",pi-pm-github-279-1126,"Round 2 (re-review): redesign the host preflight outcome table. Older-than-minimum, unreadable/prerelease launcher and unreadable/contradictory tested range still stop before tracker commands. A host NEWER than the tested ceiling no longer stops: one warning annotation plus one job-summary line ('pm CLI X is newer than the newest host this pm-github release was tested with (Y); continuing. If the apply step fails, <remedy>'), then preview/apply continue. A later apply or closeout-write failure leads its message and the sync alert body with that same hint (both versions and remedy) before the preserved underlying error. A release may declare a reviewed known-incompatible host ('pmCliIncompatibleFrom' in package.json, absent by default, must be a stable version above the tested ceiling; only hosts at or above it stop). The JSON diagnostic carries case: below_minimum, supported, newer_untested, declared_incompatible, unreadable (supported stays a fully silent pass, so the pass itself emits no JSON). The CodeRabbit thread at pm-github-closeout.yml:334 is fixed by making every remedy hold-aware: when pm-github-version selects the release, callers are told to remove or update that hold, or move the workflow pin after dropping it; the no-hold remedy keeps the workflow-pin wording. Fixing the whole class: both reusable workflows (byte-identical preflight shells), the shared failure reporter, the sync alert body, README, both caller templates and the recovery doc."
  "2026-11-26T11:24:03.194Z",pi-pm-github-279-1126,"Round 2 implementation complete. Outcome table now enforced in both reusable workflows (byte-identical preflight shells, verified by the publication suite): below_minimum stops, supported stays a fully silent pass (no JSON, no summary), newer_untested emits exactly one warning annotation plus one job-summary line, writes pm-cli-host-compatibility-hint and the host_compatibility step output, and continues; declared_incompatible stops only at or above the release's reviewed pmCliIncompatibleFrom metadata value (absent here; a declaration at or below the tested ceiling or an unstable value fails closed as an unreadable range); unreadable covers missing/failing/malformed launchers, prerelease hosts and unreadable/contradictory ranges. Every remedy is hold-aware (CodeRabbit thread on pm-github-closeout.yml:334): when pm-github-version selects the release, callers are told to remove or update that hold, or move the workflow pin after dropping it; hold-free callers keep the plain workflow-pin remedy. The shared failure reporter now leads any post-preflight failure message with the newer-host hint before the preserved underlying error, and the sync alert body leads with the same validated hint (regex-anchored, newline-free) before the failing step. The preflight JSON diagnostic carries case: below_minimum / supported / newer_untested / declared_incompatible / unreadable (supported emits no JSON at all by design; a silent pass is asserted byte-exact)."
  "2026-11-26T11:24:12.740Z",pi-pm-github-279-1126,"Revert proofs (disposable copy, original worktree untouched). Revert 1 - both reusable workflows restored to the previous head (newer-than-tested host still stopped, old report vocabulary, no hint transport): 37 of 57 tests fail, including 'sync/closeout compatibility preflight: newer untested host' and 'the fleet pair passes with the warning' (the stop-versus-warn decision), 'declared known-incompatible host', 'apply failures lead with the newer-host hint', and the alert hint-body test; the silent-pass scenarios keep passing as before. Revert 2 - only the hold detection disabled (hold = false) in both workflows: exactly the six hold scenarios fail for both sync and closeout (older host, newer untested host, missing local launcher, each with an explicit hold), proving every hold-set remedy names the pm-github-version hold. No existing test was weakened or deleted; every prior round-1 scenario retains a stricter assertion."
  "2026-11-26T12:01:16.836Z",pi-pm-github-279-1126,"Round 2 gates (all local, exact worktree): typecheck, eslint, docstring gate (31 files, 322 declarations), privacy gate (10590 objects, no matches), identity inventory --check, changelog:full + changelog:check (unchanged), and verify-release-publish-attestation all pass after a full build. Focused extract-and-run suites: workflow-host-compatibility 45/45, daily-sync-alert + package-metadata 18/18, closeout-workflow-publication 33/33 (both preflight shells byte-identical), self-versioned-workflows + the focused set 127/127, verify-release-publish-attestation + identity-inventory + round-twelve 45/45. Recorded selection: import-gate 54/54 and the remaining 34 selection files 1149/1149, zero failures, concurrency 2. Coverage and the npm/Bun release gates are delegated to exact-head CI at unchanged thresholds."
